/-
  OIBridge/StructuralClosure.lean — the substratum-source audit, fourth entry: structural
  closure of the substratum architecture.

  ROUND SIXTY-FOUR. Round 61 reduced the primitive-source question to one object — a quantum
  architecture: an implementation class closed under the theory operations, context-stable,
  label-invariant, dagger-stable, and driving the elementary transitions. Rounds 62 and 63
  settled the decisive fifth ingredient for the current axioms: the substratum supplies only
  monomial operators, and read-write coupling does not supply the off-diagonal generator. This
  file audits the FOUR STRUCTURAL ingredients for the class the substratum actually supplies,
  and returns the honest answer for each: all four close, and nothing is completed by
  definition.

  THE CLASS IS THE SUPPLIED CLASS, NOT A HULL. The round-62 interface records that the
  substratum's direct interventions — bijective dynamics (A2) and phase — and the round-63
  read-write couplings have monomial observable operators: `permMatrix σ * diagonal d`, a
  permutation of a diagonal, the weights permitted to vanish (as the readout projectors
  require). The substratum class of this file (`substratumClass`) is exactly that predicate,
  `IsMonomial`, so every operator in it is supplied by an intervention followed by a diagonal
  weighting, and no operator is added to obtain closure.

  THE ELEMENTWISE FORM. A matrix is monomial if and only if it has at most one nonzero entry in
  every row and in every column (`IsSubmonomial`, `monomial_iff_submonomial`). The direction
  monomial ⇒ submonomial is a reading of the entries; the converse extends the partial injection
  "column ↦ row of its nonzero entry" to a permutation of the finite carrier by matching the
  complements, which have equal cardinality. The elementwise form is what makes the closure
  audit a computation on entries rather than on permutations.

  THE FOUR CLOSURES.
    (1) ARCHITECTURE CLOSURE — the identity is monomial, a product of monomials is monomial (a
        nonzero entry of `K * L` picks one nonzero entry of `K` and one of `L`, and the row and
        column conditions of each transfer), scalar multiples are monomial, the readout
        projectors are diagonal, and every ancilla block of a monomial is monomial
        (`substratumClass_arch`).
    (2) CONTEXT STABILITY — `1_R ⊗ K` has a nonzero entry only where the spectator indices
        agree and `K` is nonzero (`substratumClass_contextStable`).
    (3) LABEL INVARIANCE — relabelling a carrier permutes rows and columns together
        (`substratumClass_labelInvariant`).
    (4) DAGGER STABILITY — the adjoint exchanges the row and column conditions
        (`substratumClass_daggerStable`); physically, the reversal of a bijective intervention
        is the inverse bijection (`bijectiveOperator_conjTranspose`) and the reversal of a phase
        is its conjugate (`phaseOperator_conjTranspose`), both of which A2 and the phase
        structure supply.

  THE RESIDUAL. For a structurally closed class, being a quantum architecture is exactly
  driving the elementary transitions (`quantumArchitecture_iff_drives_of_closed`). The
  substratum class is structurally closed but generates no composite unitary control — every
  monomial conjugation preserves the diagonal and the rotation `rot` does not — so its
  generated theory is not quantum mechanics (`substratumGen_not_qm`), it does not drive the
  elementary transitions (`substratumClass_not_drivesElementary`), and it is not a quantum
  architecture (`substratumClass_not_quantumArchitecture`). The closure audit therefore returns
  `substratum_residual`: four closures, one residual, and the residual is exactly the
  off-diagonal controllability that rounds 62 and 63 showed the current axioms do not supply.

  THE ENDPOINT. Any structurally closed extension of the substratum class is a quantum
  architecture exactly when it drives the elementary transitions
  (`substratum_extension_quantum_iff_drives`); such an extension generates finite operational
  quantum mechanics on every nonempty carrier (`substratum_plus_control_qm`); and finite
  operational quantum mechanics is generated by a quantum architecture extending the substratum
  class (`qm_generated_by_substratum_extension`). In one line:

      ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
      │  current OI substratum + continuous off-diagonal controllability             │
      │      ⟺  finite operational quantum mechanics.                                 │
      └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. No operation is supplied by fiat: the class is the round-62 predicate
  and every closure is a theorem about it. The controllability side of the endpoint is a
  hypothesis on an extension, not a property of the current substratum — the current substratum
  does not have it (`substratumClass_not_drivesElementary`), and no control law is postulated to
  obtain it. Nothing here modifies the frozen OI⁺ statements. The compact-semigroup redundancy of
  the inverse clause and the minimal elementary repertoire remain open.
-/

